<para id="RM00000211V00LX" category="C" type-id="3034A" name-id="066O3-00" from="200708">
<dtccode>P0516</dtccode>
<dtcname>Battery Temperature Sensor (Low)</dtcname>
<dtccode>P0517</dtccode>
<dtcname>Battery Temperature Sensor (High)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM00000211V00LX_05" type-id="31" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000D9100000">
<name>Circuit Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The battery thermometer sensor detects the battery temperature. The resistance of the thermistor built into the battery thermometer sensor changes in accordance with changes in the battery temperature. The lower the battery temperature, the higher the thermistor resistance; conversely, the higher the temperature, the lower the resistance. The battery thermometer sensor is connected to the engine control computer, and a power supply voltage of 5V is supplied to the battery thermometer sensor from terminal THB of the engine control computer via resistor R. In other words, since resistor R and the battery thermometer sensor are connected in series, the resistance changes in accordance with changes in the battery temperature, and the potential at terminal THB also changes. Based on this signal, the engine control computer reduces the charging current when the battery temperature is high, to protect the battery.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="A080941J03" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
